  "behavior": [
    "TON import serializes with seed recovery/export and master-password change. It reads the live password when the operation runs and rejects locked imports rather than returning an unstored address.",
    "Import reads the durable record first. Existing records retain name, metadata, unknown fields and ciphertext when already usable. Only a verified matching phrase repairs an inaccessible seed, preserving the rest of the record.",
    "New seeds are encrypted and decrypted/verified against the derived public key before a conditional no-overwrite store update. The account becomes visible and creation succeeds only after storage acknowledgement; read/write failures reject and allow explicit retry.",
    "Concurrent imports preserve the first durable record. An import before password change is included in staging; an import after the change begins waits and encrypts with the new password.",
    "New import and explicit recovery own their awaited write errors, avoiding replay of handled failures by a later global password-write flush. Other legacy void-write tracking is unchanged.",
    "A lock during an in-flight write leaves its committed ciphertext recoverable but rejects late completion; unlock and explicit retry reuse it. The real Extension creation message awaits the seed write before selecting the account. Existing Vue pending/failure/retry behavior is regression-tested without presentation changes."
  ],
