        "path": "src/extension/background/extension-base/src/services/keyring-service/TonSeedVault.ts",
        "line": 122,
        "description": "A fresh import validates password before the store transform, then awaits durable commit without a final live-password check. Locking while the write is pending still returns success; Extension.accountsCreate then selects the account. The already-committed encrypted record must remain, but stale import completion must reject.",
        "status": "Root reproduced the failure at 3ad08af8; fe2d86c1 adds a final live-password equality check after the awaited write. The actual Extension regression asserts rejection, no selection, retained decryptable committed record and exact-record reuse after unlock/retry. Independent follow-up source review finds this correction addresses the reported commit-window race."
      }
    ],
    "remainingScopedBlockers": [],
    "otherDisposition": [
      "Import and password changes share the vault queue, and password is read when the queued operation starts.",
      "A durable pre-existing record owns its address and metadata; conflicting keys fail and conditional create avoids overwriting a late record.",
      "New and recovered ciphertext is verified against the expected public key before persistence; publication follows acknowledged writes.",
      "Awaited fresh/recovery writes opt out of the fire-and-forget failure accumulator, so their handled errors do not poison later password flushes.",
      "Actual Chrome and Web adapter constructor assertions plus live IS_EXTENSION getter correct the old cached mock that mislabeled Chrome coverage as IndexedDB."
